data: {"type":"data-source","data":{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/frontend-modules/overview.mdx","name":"overview.mdx","revision":"HEAD"}}

data: {"type":"tool-output-available","toolCallId":"call-8ef1ae53-e28a-4d51-a441-4b06640cc901","output":{"output":"<repo>github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs</repo>\n<path>content/en-US/docs/frontend-modules/overview.mdx</path>\n<url>undefined</url>\n<content>\n180:     \"vitest\": \"^4.1.2\"\n181:   },\n182:   \"packageManager\": \"yarn@4.10.3\"\n183: }\n184: ```\n185: \n186: Some key things to note from looking at this file include:\n187: \n188: - The `name` property which defines the name of the module. This property is used as the module’s unique identifier in the [import map](/docs/core-concepts#import-map).\n189: - The `browser` property which points to the entry point of the built bundle that gets served (what the app shell loads at runtime).\n190: - The `main` property which defines the [entry point](#the-application-entry-point-indexts) of the frontend module’s source code, which is typically `src/index.ts`.\n191: - The OpenMRS runtime packages are usually peer dependencies for consumers and `next` dev dependencies for local development.\n192: - `@carbon/react` is a `1.x` peer dependency so that the build shares the app shell's copy instead of bundling its own. A copy in `devDependencies` provides types and lets tests run.\n193: - The Rspack config and CLI packages are dev dependencies because they are build-time tooling, not runtime modules loaded by the app shell.\n194: - ESLint 9 and `@openmrs/eslint-config` are dev dependencies. Shared rules and repository-specific ignores live in the root `eslint.config.mjs`; see [Linting](/docs/frontend-modules/development#linting).\n195: - Current React frontend modules use Rspack and Vitest by default. Older modules may still have Webpack or Jest scripts while they are being migrated.\n196: \n197: ### The application entry point (`index.ts`)\n198: \n199: Frontend modules define their entry point in `src/index.ts`.\n200: \n201: ```ts\n202: import { defineConfigSchema, getAsyncLifecycle, getSyncLifecycle } from \"@openmrs/esm-framework\";\n203: import { configSchema } from \"./config-schema\";\n204: import ActivePrescriptionsSummary from \"./active-prescriptions-summary.component\";\n205: import { moduleName } from \"./constants\";\n206: \n207: export const importTranslation = require.context(\"../translations\", false, /.json$/, \"lazy\");\n208: \n209: const options = {\n210:   featureName: \"active-prescriptions\",\n211:   moduleName,\n212: };\n213: \n214: export function startupApp() {\n215:   defineConfigSchema(moduleName, configSchema);\n216: }\n217: \n218: export const root = getAsyncLifecycle(() => import(\"./root.component\"), options);\n219: \n220: export const activePrescriptionsSummary = getSyncLifecycle(ActivePrescriptionsSummary, options);\n221: ```\n222: \n223: This file is the entry point of the frontend module. It is the first file that gets executed when the frontend module gets loaded. It is responsible for setting up the frontend module and exporting the module’s configuration. Specifically, in this example:\n224: \n225: - It exports an `importTranslation` function which is used to load the module’s translations.\n226: - It also exports two named lifecycle functions, `root` and `activePrescriptionsSummary`. These names must match the component names declared in `routes.json`. The app shell calls them when the corresponding page or extension needs to render.\n227: - It also exports a `startupApp` function which is used to set up the frontend module. In this case, the frontend module's configuration schema is defined here. Modules that need breadcrumbs or other framework registration can do that in `startupApp` too.\n228: \n229: #### The `startupApp` function\n230: \n231: Many frontend modules define a function named `startupApp`. This function performs setup that should happen once, immediately before the module's first page, extension, modal, or workspace lifecycle is loaded. The `startupApp` function is where we commonly:\n232: \n233: - define the module's configuration schema\n234: - register breadcrumbs\n235: - run other load-time setup that must happen before the module's exported lifecycles are used\n236: \n237: Page and extension registration itself comes from `routes.json`, not from `startupApp`. If a module does not need load-time setup, `startupApp` can be omitted.\n238: \n239: #### The `importTranslation` function\n240: \n241: This is required when the module provides translations. It tells the frontend application how to load translation strings. Note that the first argument to `require.context` is a directory, `../translations`. That directory must exist at that location relative to the `index.ts` file.\n242: \n243: ### Static metadata in `routes.json`\n244: \n245: The `routes.json` file is used to set up the frontend module's static metadata. These include:\n246: \n247: - The `pages` that the frontend module provides\n248: - The `extensions` that the frontend module provides\n249: - The `modals`, `workspaces`, `workspaceGroups`, and `featureFlags` that the frontend module provides\n250: - The `backendDependencies` that the frontend module requires. This object tells the frontend application what OpenMRS server modules the frontend module depends on, and what versions. If these dependencies are not met, administrators will be alerted\n251: \n252: The structure of this static file is dictated by the OpenMRS Routes standard [JSON schema](https://json.openmrs.org/routes.schema.json).\n253: \n254: Before shipping a new page or extension, check whether `routes.json` should also declare:\n255: \n256: - `backendDependencies` or `optionalBackendDependencies` for required backend modules.\n257: - `privileges` for role-based access to an extension.\n258: - `featureFlags` and per-extension `featureFlag` values for work that should be hidden until enabled.\n\n(Output capped at 5KB. Showing lines 180-258 of 320. Use offset=259 to continue.)\n</content>","sources":[{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/frontend-modules/overview.mdx","name":"overview.mdx","revision":"HEAD"}]}}

