data: {"type":"data-source","data":{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/configuration-system.mdx","name":"configuration-system.mdx","revision":"HEAD"}}

data: {"type":"tool-output-available","toolCallId":"call-1dbcdb7a-b0ac-4733-a6cd-b003e5bc0dc0","output":{"output":"<repo>github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs</repo>\n<path>content/en-US/docs/configuration-system.mdx</path>\n<url>undefined</url>\n<content>\n337: #### Extension-specific configuration\n338: \n339: Extensions can have their own configuration schemas that are separate from their parent module's configuration. This is useful when an extension needs configuration options that don't apply to the module as a whole.\n340: \n341: To define an extension-specific config schema, use `defineExtensionConfigSchema`:\n342: \n343: ```ts\n344: import { defineExtensionConfigSchema, Type } from \"@openmrs/esm-framework\";\n345: \n346: export function startupApp() {\n347:   defineExtensionConfigSchema(\"my-extension-name\", {\n348:     customSetting: {\n349:       _type: Type.String,\n350:       _default: \"default value\",\n351:       _description: \"A setting specific to this extension\"\n352:     }\n353:   });\n354: }\n355: ```\n356: \n357: The extension name should match the `name` property of the extension as defined in `routes.json`. When an extension has its own config schema, base values for that schema are provided under the extension name, not under the module name. `useConfig()` within that extension still returns the module's normal configuration plus the extension's configuration. Extension-specific values take precedence when the same top-level key exists in both places.\n358: \n359: **How extension configuration is resolved:**\n360: \n361: Extension configuration values are determined by merging multiple sources in this order:\n362: \n363: 1. **Extension's base configuration** - Values provided under the extension name when the extension has its own schema, or under the extension module name when it uses the module schema\n364: 2. **Slot-specific overrides** - Values from the `configure` object in the slot's configuration (highest precedence)\n365: \n366: This merging allows administrators to customize an extension's behavior differently for each slot where it appears. For example, the same extension could have different settings when used in a patient header versus a dashboard.\n367: \n368: The `configure` key must match the extension ID assigned to the slot. If you attach the same extension multiple times with instance IDs such as `my-extension#left` and `my-extension#right`, configure those full IDs separately.\n369: \n370: For example, this provides the extension's base configuration:\n371: \n372: ```json\n373: {\n374:   \"my-extension-name\": {\n375:     \"customSetting\": \"base value\"\n376:   }\n377: }\n378: ```\n379: \n380: Extension configuration can then be overridden per-slot using the `configure` object in the slot's configuration:\n381: \n382: ```json\n383: {\n384:   \"@openmrs/esm-my-module\": {\n385:     \"extensionSlots\": {\n386:       \"my-slot\": {\n387:         \"configure\": {\n388:           \"my-extension-name\": {\n389:             \"customSetting\": \"slot-specific value\"\n390:           }\n391:         }\n392:       }\n393:     }\n394:   }\n395: }\n396: ```\n397: \n398: ## Schema Reference\n399: \n400: `_default`\n401: \n402: All config elements must have a default (excluding elements within arrays or freeform objects governed by `_elements`).\n403: \n404: The default does not necessarily need to satisfy the `_type` or the `_validators` of the element, but this may change in future versions.\n405: \n406: `_type`\n407: \n408: One of the values from the Type enum. Used for validation and to help the implementer tools work with the element.\n409: \n410: Should always appear alongside `_default`.\n411: \n412: `_description`\n413: \n414: Helps implementers understand what the configuration element actually does and how it is intended to be used.\n415: \n416: Can be used anywhere within the schema structure.\n417: \n418: `_validators`\n419: \n420: An array of validator objects.\n421: \n422: Some common validators are provided, including [`inRange`](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/inRange.md), [`oneOf`](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/oneOf.md), and [`isUrlWithTemplateParameters`](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/isUrlWithTemplateParameters.md).\n423: \n424: Custom validators should be created with the [`validator`](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/validator.md) function.\n425: \n426: Can be used anywhere within the schema structure.\n427: \n428: `_elements`\n429: \n430: Only valid alongside `_type: Type.Array` or `_type: Type.Object`. A `_default` must also be provided at this level. For arrays, the value should be a schema for each array item. For freeform objects, the value should be a schema for each object value.\n431: \n432: ### API Documentation\n433: \n434: See the generated API docs for [`defineConfigSchema`](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/defineConfigSchema.md), [`defineExtensionConfigSchema`](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/defineExtensionConfigSchema.md), [`getConfig`](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/getConfig.md), [`useConfig`](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/useConfig.md), and [`validator`](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/validator.md).\n435: \n436: ### The RFC\n437: \n\n(Output capped at 5KB. Showing lines 337-437 of 439. Use offset=438 to continue.)\n</content>","sources":[{"type":"file","repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","path":"content/en-US/docs/configuration-system.mdx","name":"configuration-system.mdx","revision":"HEAD"}]}}

